    {
      "name": "inspect_rfem_api",
      "description": "Look up the EXACT RFEM API field names, types, enum values, AND app method signatures from the INSTALLED RFEM build — copy them verbatim into run_rfem_script. Deterministic and version-exact; works even when RFEM is NOT running (no connection needed).\n\nUse this to find the precise identifier/signature to type. For how a field is USED, worked examples, or what it MEANS in prose, use search_dlubal_apidocs instead.\n\nQuery forms:\n- Object:            inspect_rfem_api(\"LoadCase\")              -> fields with types, enums, relations\n- Object (filtered): inspect_rfem_api(\"LoadCase weight\")       -> only fields matching the term(s)\n- Enum (filtered):   inspect_rfem_api(\"ActionCategory office\") -> matching enum value names (never dumps all 400+)\n- Method:            inspect_rfem_api(\"set_base_data\")         -> the app.* method signature (e.g. keyword-only args)\n- Keyword search:    inspect_rfem_api(\"concrete addon\")        -> ranked matches across classes/fields/enums/methods\n\nExamples that prevent common mistakes:\n- inspect_rfem_api(\"concrete addon\")  -> base_data.addons.concrete_design_active\n- inspect_rfem_api(\"stress\")          -> stress_strain_analysis_active  (NOT stress_analysis_active)\n- inspect_rfem_api(\"set_base_data\")   -> set_base_data(*, base_data=..., ...) — base_data is KEYWORD-only\n- inspect_rfem_api(\"ActionCategory office\") -> the exact enum value to assign to LoadCase.action_category\n",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "query": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "query"
        ]
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "result": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "result"
        ],
        "type": "object",
        "x-fastmcp-wrap-result": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "read_rfem_results",
      "description": "Reads a bounded, typed RFEM 6 result summary without executing caller-supplied Python and without changing or recalculating the model.\n\nAllowed result types only: calculation_status, member_internal_forces, node_deformations, stability_critical_load_factors, steel_member_design_ratios.\nResult queries require explicit object_nos (except stability) and loadings (LC/CO/RC/DS identifiers). They are allowlist-validated and verified again against every returned row. Results are capped at 100 rows, sorted by the governing numeric value, carry units and a canonical result_hash, and omit model paths, object names, raw warnings and raw exceptions.\n\nPass model_guid whenever the caller is bound to a specific model. The reader resolves that exact GUID from RFEM's open-model list without changing the active model and fails closed when it is not open. Omitting model_guid retains active-model behavior for interactive compatibility.\n\nUse calculation_status first when you only need to know whether the bound model has results. A no_results or unavailable status is not a successful engineering check and must never be treated as completed.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "result_type": {
            "enum": [
              "calculation_status",
              "member_internal_forces",
              "node_deformations",
              "stability_critical_load_factors",
              "steel_member_design_ratios"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          },
          "object_nos": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "minimum": 1,
                  "type": "integer"
