    {
      "name": "run_rfem_script",
      "description": "Executes Python code against RFEM 6. Use this as the FIRST tool for any RFEM interaction — it connects internally and returns a clear error if RFEM is unreachable.\n\nAvailable objects: 'app' (RFEM Application), 'rfem' (dlubal.api.rfem module), 'math'.\nNo imports or 'with' blocks needed.\n\nexecution_id is an optional caller-generated UUID. Reusing it retrieves the same operation; changed input is rejected. context_id is an optional caller-owned chat scope. model_guid explicitly selects a model; otherwise the context reuses its remembered GUID. A 120-second wait can return running: query get_rfem_execution by ID, never replay the code. Busy/unknown operations block further scripts. Earlier changes are not rolled back on failure.\n\nCRITICAL DATA TYPES (Protobuf gRPC):\n- definition_nodes, nodes, members: ALWAYS int lists e.g. [1, 2] — NEVER strings!\n- Enum fields: full label string e.g. \"ANALYSIS_TYPE_GEOMETRICALLY_LINEAR\", \"TYPE_BEAM\"\n- load_direction: \"LOAD_DIRECTION_GLOBAL_Z_OR_USER_DEFINED_W_TRUE_LENGTH\"\n\nExample — populate a model you are authorized to modify. Inspect existing objects first; never delete them merely to recover from a failed script:\n  app.create_object(rfem.structure_core.Material(no=1, name=\"S235\"))\n  app.create_object(rfem.structure_core.CrossSection(no=1, name=\"IPE 240\", material=1))\n  app.create_object(rfem.structure_core.Node(no=1, coordinate_1=0.0, coordinate_2=0.0, coordinate_3=0.0))\n  app.create_object(rfem.structure_core.Node(no=2, coordinate_1=6.0, coordinate_2=0.0, coordinate_3=0.0))\n  app.create_object(rfem.structure_core.Line(no=1, definition_nodes=[1, 2]))\n  app.create_object(rfem.structure_core.Member(no=1, line=1, cross_section_start=1))\n  app.create_object(rfem.types_for_nodes.NodalSupport(no=1, nodes=[1], spring_x=float('inf'), spring_y=float('inf'), spring_z=float('inf')))\n  app.create_object(rfem.types_for_nodes.NodalSupport(no=2, nodes=[2], spring_y=float('inf'), spring_z=float('inf')))\n  app.create_object(rfem.loading.StaticAnalysisSettings(no=1, analysis_type=\"ANALYSIS_TYPE_GEOMETRICALLY_LINEAR\"))\n  app.create_object(rfem.loading.LoadCase(no=1, name=\"LC1\", static_analysis_settings=1, to_solve=True))\n  app.create_object(rfem.loads.MemberLoad(no=1, load_type=\"LOAD_TYPE_FORCE\", members=[1], load_case=1, load_distribution=\"LOAD_DISTRIBUTION_UNIFORM\", load_direction=\"LOAD_DIRECTION_GLOBAL_Z_OR_USER_DEFINED_W_TRUE_LENGTH\", magnitude=-10000))\n",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "code": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "execution_id": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null
          },
          "context_id": {
            "default": "",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "model_guid": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "code"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "write_rfem_model",
      "description": "Create a NEW RFEM model from bounded typed objects in dependency order. Does not execute Python, open files, delete objects or modify existing models. Use inspect_rfem_api for installed field names; fields use SDK SI units. z_axis explicitly sets and verifies the NEW model's axis before any objects are written. The resulting model_guid identifies the new model. Partial writes remain on failure; query get_rfem_execution with the same caller-owned execution_id, never replay. Rigid support fields accept the SDK JSON string 'Infinity'.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "model_name": {
            "maxLength": 128,
            "minLength": 1,
            "type": "string"
          },
          "objects": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "kind": {
                  "enum": [
                    "Material",
                    "CrossSection",
                    "Node",
                    "Line",
                    "Member",
                    "NodalSupport",
                    "StaticAnalysisSettings",
                    "LoadCase",
                    "NodalLoad",
                    "MemberLoad"
                  ],
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "no": {
                  "maximum": 1000000,
                  "minimum": 1,
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "fields": {
                  "additionalProperties": {},
                  "maxProperties": 128,
                  "type": "object"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "kind",
                "no"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            "maxItems": 1000,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array"
          },
          "z_axis": {
            "enum": [
              "up",
              "down"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          },
          "execution_id": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null
          },
          "context_id": {
            "default": "",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "model_name",
          "objects",
          "z_axis"
        ]
      }
    }
